Mic and Speaker are switches
============================

The composer carried two device dropdowns. They were a worse copy of Settings → Voice, they made the
toolbar look like a control panel, and the raw ALSA identifiers they had to show ("alsa_input.usb-
FuZhou_Kingwayinfo_CO_LTD_TONOR_TC30_Audio_Device …") are keys, not names anybody recognises.

Both are plain switches again: Mic opens the microphone, Speaker reads replies aloud, and with both
on the toolbar says Conversation. Which input and which output they use is chosen once, in Settings,
where the lists already live and where the label says what the device is.

The microphone also gets a glyph of its own. `icon()` falls back to `icons.file` for any name it does
not know, so a missing `mic` key drew a sheet of paper next to the word — a placeholder that reads as
the wrong control rather than an unfinished one.

